CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: design
SCALE_REALISM: "Partial. The q=1.0000 precision result on GSM8K/MATH-500 and zero adversarial false merges support realistic high-precision graders. However, the load-bearing MATH phi result still uses proxy answer frequencies, and the only real-model maj@k run is GSM8K, 150 problems, k=16, where Stage A predicts phi≈0 and no inversion. No shipping-scale or real symbolic-MATH model-sample inversion is demonstrated."
RATIONALE: "No OSS system I found already implements the full mechanism: existing systems implement pieces, especially Math-Verify/OpenCompass/lm-eval symbolic answer equivalence and Minerva majority voting, but not the phi-governed effect of canonicalizer recall on maj@k rankings. This is more than glue because it frames an evaluator-design hazard with a measurable asymmetry variable, but it is not a new voting mechanism: the packet itself ties it to spoiler-effect/Duverger vote splitting. Evidence supports an ecological foothold: q=1.0000 on 239,881 GSM8K and 4,983 MATH-500 merged pairs with zero over-merges, and MATH-500 proxy phi median about -1.0 to -1.2. Evidence is insufficient for green because the claimed in-the-wild ranking inversion remains simulation-only/exploratory, and real model frequencies were measured only on GSM8K where the observed null is expected."
```
